11. Understanding the Confusion Matrix

I learned how to interpret the four components of a confusion matrix:

True Negative (TN): The subscriber was predicted not to churn and actually did not churn.
False Positive (FP): The subscriber was predicted to churn but actually did not churn.
False Negative (FN): The subscriber was predicted not to churn but actually churned.
True Positive (TP): The subscriber was predicted to churn and actually churned.

I also learned that these values should be interpreted from the perspective of the retention team, not just as model statistics.

Each type of prediction has a different business impact.

